{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses: Speak to the priests.</b> What was stated above concerns understanding and instructing in all kinds of impurity, and distinguishing between the clean animal and the unclean, and between the unclean bird and the clean — for this is especially fitting for priests, as it says: וּלְהַבְדִּיל בֵּין הַקֹּדֶשׁ וּבֵין הַחֹל וּבֵין הַטָּמֵא וּבֵין הַטָּהוֹר וּלְהוֹרֹת (Leviticus 10:10–11)." "<b>And you shall say to them.</b> For they must be warned, beyond the above, also regarding corpse impurity and the profanation of seed — these being degrees of sanctity for priests alone." "<b>He shall not defile himself for a soul among his people.</b> No priest shall defile himself for a soul among his people — that is, any deceased person from the general public who is not his close relative, but is merely of his people."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:08.384848030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}